{
  "id": "80644",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Ksp and Molar Solubility Calculations",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Now we extend the discussion of "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": " to determine the molar solubility of a substance."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3ftxifzkxtag1nq",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": " of a slightly soluble ionic compound may be simply related to its measured solubility provided the dissolution process involves only dissociation and solvation. For example: "
              }
            ],
            "id": "icarsx8swzbvkyd",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "zmtceqyxoyilj2p",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "il08ll8eyavtgkx",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm Mp\\mathrm Xq(s)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;p\\mathrm M^{\\mathrm m+}(aq)\\;+\\;q\\mathrm X^{\\mathrm n-}(aq)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "For such cases, we can derive "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "sp"
              },
              {
                "text": " values from provided solubilities, or vice versa. Calculations of this sort are most conveniently performed using a compound’s molar solubility, measured as moles of dissolved solute per liter of saturated solution."
              }
            ],
            "id": "999bxog9e8a5cdi",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "981160212",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
